  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Being available – 2v2 + 2 target players",
  "description": "Two teams play 2v2 inside a square of about 12 × 12 metres. Outside the square there are four target zones, one on each side. Each team has two target players of its own standing in opposite zones – blue on the left and right, red at the top and bottom. The team with the ball is therefore four against two.\n\nA team scores when the ball travels from one of its target players to the other, through the players in the square. Playing back to the same target player to keep the ball is allowed but scores nothing. The diagram is not to scale.\n\nEasier: play 1v1 + 2. Make the square bigger or smaller to suit the players.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stand where there is a free passing lane between you and the ball carrier – not behind a defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look around before the ball arrives, so you already know where the next pass goes."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Show with your stick and your voice that you are ready for the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass to your team-mate's stick, ideally on the side away from the defender."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 2,
